## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/quantize.html
- Summary (EN): Quantize snaps input values to a set of discrete levels, reducing the number of colour levels in an image for a posterized look. Its documented input is a single source layer, and a Mask parameter blends the result with the original.
- Résumé (FR) : Ce nœud ramène les valeurs d'un calque à un nombre limité de paliers, ce qui produit un effet posterisé.

- Inputs meaning: ["source: layer to quantize; the Signature parameter sets the layer type it accepts"]

- Key parameters: ["Signature: layer type accepted by source", "Mask: blend between the quantized and original values; default 1 uses only the new value", "Method: Width and Offset, or Number of Segments", "Width: spacing between levels as a fraction of the 0 to 1 range; 0.1 gives 11 levels", "Offset: shifts where the quantization levels fall", "Segments: number of levels when using Number of Segments; 3 gives 0, 0.5 and 1", "Minimum Value / Maximum Value: the range divided into segments", "Compute Range: fills Minimum and Maximum from the source layer's actual values", "Rounding: Floor, Closest, Ceiling or Custom", "Rounding Threshold: cutoff between the two nearest levels, used only with Custom; 0, 0.5 and 1 behave like Floor, Closest and Ceiling", "Clamp Below / Clamp Above: clamp input values to Minimum or Maximum before quantizing"]

- Caveats: ["Width/Offset and Segments/Minimum/Maximum apply under different Method settings, so only the relevant fields matter for a given setup.", "Rounding Threshold has no effect unless Rounding is set to Custom.", "The page does not say how multichannel or non-layer data is handled beyond the Signature setting, and gives no performance details."]

